{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e04-scene-10",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Детектор лжи  (The Lie Detector)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "expert": "Эксперт",
  "fedya": "Федя"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The chef is determined to find the traitor, so he has hired a lie-detector expert and set up a machine in his office. Fedya, the fish cook, is the first to be questioned. Here is the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Заходи, Федя. Садись на стул.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, а что это такое?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это настоящий детектор лжи, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я должен поймать крысу на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Отвечайте только «да» или «нет».",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Хорошо, это мне вполне понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Скажите, сегодня действительно среда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, сегодня среда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Ваше настоящее имя Фёдор?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ходил в соседний ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нет, я никуда не ходил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Свободен. Позови сюда Сеню.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through the questioning.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Заходи, Федя. Садись на стул.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come in, Fedya. Sit down on the chair.' \"Zakhodi\" is \"come in\", with \"za-\", and \"sadis'\" is \"sit yourself down\", so the \"-s'\" at the end is a little \"self\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, а что это такое?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, what is this thing?' \"Chto eto takoye\" is \"what is this such\", a very handy way to ask what something is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это настоящий детектор лжи, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is a real lie detector, Fedya.' \"Lozh'\" is a lie, and \"lzhi\" is \"of a lie\", with some letters dropped. The machine's name is a phrase, \"detector of lies\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я должен поймать крысу на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I must catch the rat in the kitchen.' Russians say \"rat\" for a traitor, just as English does. \"Poymat'\" is \"to catch\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Отвечайте только «да» или «нет».",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Answer only yes or no.' \"Otvechayte\" ends in \"-te\", the ending of a command to a formal \"you\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Хорошо, это мне вполне понятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, that is completely clear to me.' \"Vpolne\" is \"in full\", so \"completely\". \"Ponyatno\" means \"it's clear\" and needs no \"I\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Скажите, сегодня действительно среда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Tell me, is today really Wednesday?' \"Sreda\" is Wednesday, and it also means \"middle\", since it's the middle of the week. \"Deystvitel'no\" is \"really\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, сегодня среда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, today is Wednesday.' Fedya answers with the same word and no verb, because Russian leaves out \"is\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Ваше настоящее имя Фёдор?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is your real name Fyodor?' The expert asks for Fedya's real name, which is the full form, \"Fyodor\", of the short \"Fedya\". \"Real\" ends in a neuter \"-oye\", because \"imya\", name, is neuter.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes.' \"Da\" is the simplest word in the scene. It's the one he is allowed to say.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ходил в соседний ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you go to the neighboring restaurant?' \"Khodil\" is \"went and came back\", the round-trip kind of \"go\". \"Sosedniy\" comes from \"sosed\", neighbour.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нет, я никуда не ходил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I did not go anywhere.' \"Nikuda\" is \"nowhere\", and with \"ne\" it's the double negative. Fedya answers with a bigger \"no\" than the question needed.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Свободен. Позови сюда Сеню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are free to go. Call Senya in here.' \"Svoboden\" is \"free\", the short form for a man. \"Pozovi\" is \"call\", a command. \"Senyu\" is the object form of \"Senya\". Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Заходи, Федя. Садись на стул.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, а что это такое?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это настоящий детектор лжи, Федя.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я должен поймать крысу на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Отвечайте только «да» или «нет».",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Хорошо, это мне вполне понятно.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Скажите, сегодня действительно среда?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да, сегодня среда.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "expert",
   "t": "Ваше настоящее имя Фёдор?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Да.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ходил в соседний ресторан?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Нет, я никуда не ходил.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Свободен. Позови сюда Сеню.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Fedya walks out of the office relieved that the machine did not catch his secrets. The word to keep is \"pravda\", truth, which you may already know.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
